Interview Answer (3 Minutes)

"In our banking project, when a payment request is received, the Payment Service publishes the event to payment-topic.

Kafka Streams consumes the event and performs multiple validations such as Fraud Validation, AML Validation, and Risk Checks. 

Once all validations pass, the event is published to validated-payment-topic. A Payment Consumer then consumes the validated event
and persists it into Oracle Database.

After successful persistence, separate events are published to payment-status-topic for callback/status updates, 
notification-topic for customer notifications, and audit-topic for regulatory audit tracking.
Any failures during processing are routed to payment-dlt for retry and investigation. 
This event-driven architecture provides loose coupling, scalability, 
fault tolerance, auditability, and regulatory compliance, which are critical requirements in banking systems like MUFG and JPMC." 🚀
